{
  "format": "souls-form-cases/1",
  "about": "eden:sand_garden (from #1678). Four cells of sand (back left, back right, front left, front right, in the garden's own frame with its stand at the front), each smooth, brushed along or brushed across. Anyone with a free hand brushes a chosen cell a chosen way (one form, `brush`: its `cell` argument is one of the four cell fields and its `pattern` one of along and across, each from the form's own list), ten seconds of work, or smooths all four. Refused, as the original refused: a cell that already has that furrow direction ('That cell already has this furrow direction.'), whose fix is the other direction, and no free hand ('Put down what you are holding before brushing the sand.'). and smoothing sand that is already smooth ('The sand is already smooth.', by `says`: a need that at least one of the four cells is not smooth). Brushing a cell smooth is not a choice of `brush` (bad input): smoothing is its own form.",
